            <ArticleTitle>[Lipid composition of mononuclear and polymorphonuclear leukocytes from peripheral blood of patients with chronic ischemic heart disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>11-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In patients with chronic heart ischemic disease increase in contents of total lipids, total, free and ester-bound cholesterol, phospholipids, free fatty acids and triglycerides was detected in mononuclear leukocytes; in polymorphonuclear leukocytes from peripheric blood of the patients increase in content of phospholipids with simultaneous decrease of free fatty acids and triglycerides were observed as compared with the similar patterns of lipid composition in the cells of healthy persons.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
